WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:00.633
Turned to

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.534
retired Army Four-Star

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.403
General Wesley Clark for insight.

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:03.870
In addition

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.471
to being a CNN

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:05.238
military analyst,

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.306
he's also a former NATO

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:08.608
supreme allied commander.

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:09.809
General Clark

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:10.944
you see the news out of Ukraine.

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:11.578
What does it say to you

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:12.545
about the effectiveness

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:13.813
of the Patriot systems

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:15.548
versus Russia's hypersonic missiles?

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:15.915
Because, I mean,

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:16.716
they had been touted

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.852
as being nearly impossible to intercept

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:21.721
Well, that's what Mr.

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:22.822
Putin said.

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.391
But it turns out that the Patriot

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:26.226
can intercept a hypersonic missile.

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:26.593
After all,

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:28.461
the Patriot was designed

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:30.330
to intercept ballistic missiles

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.431
that were incoming.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:31.798
And so

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:34.034
they're moving at much more than three

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:36.002
or four times the speed of sound.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.171
So the Patriot has a radar,

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.139
the guidance system

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:41.241
and the energy and the missile

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:42.609
to be able to strike

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:44.310
an incoming hypersonic missile.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:44.744
Do you know,

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.446
I mean, how large Russia supply

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:47.680
these hypersonic missiles is?

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.282
I mean, cannot afford to keep

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:51.751
using them in waves of attack

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:55.188
I think it

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:56.122
is really

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.991
a logistics issue for both sides.

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:59.325
The question is,

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:00.927
how many Patriot missiles

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.996
can Ukraine afford to fire?

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:04.297
And as I look at it,

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:05.932
Anderson, is a sort of strategic

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:07.233
calculus by the Russians

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.169
to try to exhaust the Ukrainians air

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:10.637
defense missiles

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:11.071
prior

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:12.772
to the time that Ukraine launches

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.207
its main attack

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:15.542
so that Russia can deploy

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.010
its tactical aircraft

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.611
and an air to ground roll

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:21.114
against the Ukrainian counteroffensive

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:21.881
we sell.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:22.916
We saw the founder

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:23.316
the Wagner

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:24.751
group claim that an American fighter

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.820
had been killed in Bermuda.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:27.554
Do you think Russia's

00:01:27.554 --> 00:01:29.222
made a mistake focusing

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:31.491
so much of its forces on Bermuda?

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:32.792
I mean, not only the Viognier group

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:35.161
but Russia's main army as well,

00:01:37.197 --> 00:01:38.398
Well, it certainly seems to me

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:39.232
like a mistake.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:41.701
We may never know why

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:42.302
they did it,

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:42.869
but it seems

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:45.004
that it's become a symbolic objective.

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.140
And the Russian high

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.442
command has obviously told its generals,

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:50.577
take back,

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:52.912
I don't care what it costs, just get it.

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:55.381
And so they've thrown

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.117
countless assaults in there.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.852
They've taken a lot of losses,

00:01:58.852 --> 00:01:59.986
and now they're vulnerable

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.688
to being actually encircled

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:02.956
by the Ukrainians.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:06.092
And this would be a huge symbolic defeat

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.060
for Russia.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:11.131
It might open the way to a surprise

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.632
offensive that goes right

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.834
through moot by the Ukrainians

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.936
at the heart of the Russian positions.

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.505
What do you think

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:19.672
a Ukrainian offensive

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.674
will hope to accomplish?

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:26.646
Ideally, the Ukrainians are going to get

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:29.282
the offensive going in the south

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:31.451
toward Crimea.

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:34.020
But we have to be prepared to be sure

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:36.156
there's going to be more than one

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:37.524
axis of attack.

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:38.691
There may be one in the north,

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.360
one of the one in the east

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.629
or dark mood or Donetsk

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.531
and then one in the south, perhaps

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:45.698
a military pole,

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:48.001
or maybe they'll go across the Dnieper

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:48.801
Retired U.S.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.303
Air Force colonel and CNN military

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.804
analyst Cedric Leighton joins us now

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:52.438
from Washington.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:53.840
Colonel, good to see you.

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:55.642
Good to see you, too, John.

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:56.609
Okay, so these hypersonic

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:57.544
Russian missiles,

00:02:57.544 --> 00:02:58.411
which are fighter key

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.345
known as console

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:01.481
or that's Russian to dagger,

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:03.449
one of Moscow's most advanced weapons,

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:04.918
which Vladimir Putin claimed

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:06.653
would overcome all existing

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:07.320
and prospective

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.988
anti-aircraft and anti-missile

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:10.557
defense systems.

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:11.691
So for Ukraine

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.593
to say they intercepted six

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:14.594
during the same exact

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:15.962
six with one blow

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:18.298
seems either incredible or incredulous

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:18.932
What are the chances

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:19.799
that Ukrainian air defenses

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:20.700
are able to take out

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.568
the hypersonic missiles,

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:22.468
which in the past

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:23.469
was considered possible,

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.038
but only in theory?

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:27.774
Well, perhaps the hypersonic missiles

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:29.509
aren't really hypersonic. John.

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:30.476
And so that's something

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:32.612
that we're going to have to examine.

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.280
You know, the Russians, of course,

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.282
have touted the capabilities

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:37.684
of the commercial missile force

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:38.851
several years now.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.086
And in the West,

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:43.056
we believe that it was a very effective,

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:44.958
highly useful weapon

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:47.393
that was, in essence, a game changer.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.062
In the field of ballistic missiles.

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:51.097
But in this particular case,

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:52.498
I think that

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:53.399
what we're seeing

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:54.200
is something

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.568
that the commercial was

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:56.669
less than meets the eye

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:58.538
and if it's true,

00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:00.173
the Ukrainians were able to shoot down

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:01.207
six of them.

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:02.842
That's a significant dent

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.444
in the purported

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:06.512
Russian inventory of commercial missiles.

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.880
Which was supposedly somewhere

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.082
around 50 or so,

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:11.117
according to Ukrainian intelligence.

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:13.519
So what did he was fired at Kiev

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.121
by the Russians.

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.656
It wasn't the hypersonic was a sort of

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:17.890
old wine in the new bottle.

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:20.460
Yeah, I think

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.061
I think that's possibly the case.

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:24.130
I think that what we may have seen

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.865
is that

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:26.466
it has

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:29.202
perhaps some hypersonic capabilities.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.536
I could still go for

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:32.872
this could still be a supersonic missile,

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:34.641
but I'm sure the missile was not going

00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:36.276
ten times the speed of sound,

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:37.977
which would have been the maximum speed

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:39.846
advertised for the chemical.

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:40.647
It will slow the Kremlin.

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:41.414
The attack on Kiev

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:42.515
using a combination of air,

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:43.549
sea and land based

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:45.184
missiles and drones was,

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:46.552
as you would expect.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:47.820
It was a complete success.

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:48.855
Listen to this.

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:51.057
Senator, go to this.

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:53.192
The purpose of the strike was achieved.

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:55.828
All the signed objects are hit.

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:57.030
A high precision strike

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:59.565
by a hypersonic missile system dagger

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:02.235
in the city of Keefe, a U.S.

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:04.437
made Patriot anti-aircraft missile

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:05.571
system was hit

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:09.342
so eight missiles were fired.

00:05:09.342 --> 00:05:10.443
Ballistic and supersonic,

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:11.811
maybe hypersonic.

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:12.745
The end result of some damage

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:14.080
to a Patriot defense system.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.815
And that's been confirmed by the US.

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:16.683
That doesn't seem good.

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:16.949
Bang.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:19.452
For your buck at the end of the day.

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:20.353
No, not at all.

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:20.987
And in fact,

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:23.156
the Russians seem to have had a

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:25.525
huge difficulty, a huge problem

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:26.726
in achieving

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:28.227
the target list that they were

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:30.463
that they were reportedly hitting.

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:30.863
So they

00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:32.665
I don't think they were very successful.

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:35.168
It's pretty clear that they achieved some

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:36.869
degree of damage

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:38.037
in certain areas,

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:38.838
including partly

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:41.074
the Patriot system, like you mentioned.

00:05:41.074 --> 00:05:42.475
But it is nowhere near

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:44.310
what they were supposed

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:48.247
what the spokesman out of Moscow said.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:48.948
And all the time

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:50.149
the Ukrainian president continues

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:51.884
to press for these F-16 fighter jets.

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:53.152
He says they're needed

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:54.721
to secure Ukraine's airspace

00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:55.755
to repeat performance

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:57.090
of what happened on Tuesday.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:57.623
To that end,

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:59.359
Downing Street released a statement.

00:05:59.359 --> 00:05:59.659
U.K.

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:00.793
Prime Minister Sunak and Dutch

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:01.260
Prime Minister

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.195
Ruiter agreed

00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:03.029
